<title>HUNGARY: Hungary one-month bill yield falls to 21.15 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary one-month bill yield falls to 21.15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of one-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 21.15 percent, down from 21.61 percent at an auction one week ago, the National Bank of Hungary said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow, and on  HTBM.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     1,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	5,407.16 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    1,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 1,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    21.15 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     98.4034 pct</p>
</text>
